Today is Tuesday.
In the evening, I call a beauty parlor.
A woman answers the phone.
She speaks very politely.
"Hello, beauty parlor," she says.
"Hello, I want a haircut," I say.
"Certainly, which day are you coming?" she asks.
"I will come on Thursday," I say.
"Okay, at what time on Thursday?" she asks.
I look at my calendar.
I am sometimes busy in the morning.
But I am free in the evening every day.
"Can I come at five thirty in the evening?" I ask.
"You can come at five thirty on Thursday evening," she says.
"What is your name?" she asks.
"My name is Maya," I say.
"Okay Maya, see you on Thursday," she says.
I hang up the phone.
I write the new time in my calendar.
